# Local to `learnings/`, in addition to the repository root's entries.
#
# Duplicating `quarantine/` here is deliberate rather than sloppy. The root
# `.gitignore` is edited by everyone and for every reason; this file is edited
# only by someone already thinking about the learning loop. If the root entry is
# ever dropped by accident, this one still stands between a quarantined
# candidate and a public commit -- and a quarantined candidate is, by
# definition, one that matched a redaction class.

# Candidates held for human review because they matched a compiled regex class.
# Never committed. A human reads them locally, then either rewrites the entry or
# adds the offending string to `redaction/denylist.txt`.
#
# Note that git does not descend into an excluded directory, so no `.gitkeep`
# inside it can be tracked from here or from the root. The directory is created
# on demand by `sdlc-suite/tools/distil.py`, and its absence is normal.
quarantine/

# The high-water mark of the last successful `--emit`. Instance state: it
# records which run outcomes this checkout has already read, which is
# meaningless in anyone else's clone and changes on every run.
.last-distil

# Everything else here IS committed, and that is the point:
#
#   learnings/*.md            ratified learnings, merged by a human
#   learnings/candidates/     proposed by the distiller, the body of its PR
#   learnings/retired/        unconfirmed for 180 days, moved by the decay pass
#
# Loading is a plain directory scan with no index and no cache, so reverting the
# merge commit removes the behaviour completely. That is why there is no
# generated manifest here to keep in step.
